{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fa78b74b-fbc6-48fe-bf46-b77c50fd8048","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0f45f0c336a6948","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-pgpp1i0v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E002.md","content":"# Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic turns the ROCm build of the vLLM serving runtime into a supported,\nproductized runtime for the models the validation campaign clears. Upstream\nvLLM publishes ROCm support and ROCm builds exist upstream, but the platform\nships and supports only CUDA runtime builds today. This epic delivers the\nproductized ROCm runtime image and its release through the platform release\nprocess.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build the ROCm variant of the vLLM serving runtime in the midstream build\n  and release pipeline, following the existing CUDA runtime builds as the\n  pattern.\n- Release the runtime image through the platform release process, scoped to\n  the model list cleared by the validation campaign.\n- Pin the base ROCm image and document how upstream ROCm runtime image\n  releases align with platform release trains.\n- License scanning of the ROCm runtime image, covering the new AMD/ROCm\n  transitive dependencies the build introduces.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The ROCm vLLM runtime image builds and its build/test/release pipeline\n  completes green.\n- The runtime image is published through the platform release process for the\n  cleared model set.\n- The runtime serves each cleared model successfully on AMD Instinct hardware,\n  with functional checks recorded per model.\n- The base ROCm image is pinned, and a documented release-alignment note\n  states how upstream ROCm image cadence maps to platform release trains.\n- The license scan of the ROCm runtime image passes, or any exceptions are\n  documented and approved.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears — this epic delivers the runtime\n  image itself; the serving-stack exposure that makes it deployable is a\n  separate unit of work on the KServe side.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Gated on the validation campaign outcome: this epic proceeds with the\n  cleared model list; a full no-go removes the productization scope.\n- Upstream ROCm build cadence is outside our control and may not align with\n  release trains; recorded as a schedule risk and addressed by the pinning\n  and release-alignment acceptance criterion above.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51504,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab044e5d9d10986e","agent_id":"a11b7706a09d57009","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"43f1bf29-a3aa-4f8f-a514-41ff614b3173","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:29:50.997Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
