{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-0f497ba8-94d7-4190-aea7-1f467c6e1c13","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-95a29d6baea1bbbe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9020-pgpp1i0v/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9020-E003.md","content":"# KServe serving-stack enablement for AMD GPU (ROCm) serving\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the serving-stack side of AMD GPU enablement: the changes\nneeded for the KServe serving stack to deploy and serve models on the ROCm\nvLLM runtime on AMD Instinct nodes — exposing the runtime as a deployable\nserving runtime, handling AMD accelerator resources, and validating\nInferenceServices end to end on AMD hardware.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Serving-stack changes required to expose the ROCm vLLM runtime as a\n  supported deployable runtime (runtime registration in the serving stack).\n- AMD accelerator resource handling in the serving stack so that inference\n  workloads requesting AMD GPU resources are scheduled onto AMD Instinct\n  nodes.\n- End-to-end validation: deploying and serving InferenceServices that use the\n  ROCm runtime on AMD Instinct hardware.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The serving stack exposes the ROCm vLLM runtime as a deployable runtime,\n  referencing the pinned productized ROCm runtime image (the image is\n  produced by the runtime productization work; its availability is an\n  acceptance gate here, not a blocking dependency).\n- An InferenceService deploying a cleared model on the ROCm runtime reaches\n  Ready and serves inference requests successfully on AMD Instinct nodes.\n- InferenceService pods requesting AMD GPU resources are scheduled and run on\n  AMD Instinct nodes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the\n  models the validation campaign clears — this epic covers the serving-stack\n  integration that makes the productized runtime deployable and usable end\n  to end.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Gated on the validation campaign outcome: scope follows the cleared model\n  list; a full no-go removes this scope.\n- The strategy lists KServe as an affected component without detailing the\n  change; this epic is scoped at the functional level (runtime exposure and\n  accelerator resource handling), leaving implementation decisions to the\n  team.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52173,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab044e5d9d10986e","agent_id":"a11b7706a09d57009","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"5f92f119-cd03-4adc-a23d-dfbe4c4a836c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:29:58.349Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9020"}
