{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9113c81627934fc9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E001\n3\ttitle: AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Serving Runtimes\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -2\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic delivers the first-hand functional and performance parity data for\n30\tvLLM serving on AMD Instinct accelerators (ROCm) that the platform currently\n31\tlacks — today only CUDA (NVIDIA) runtime builds are productized and no\n32\tfirst-hand AMD data exists for the supported model set. It runs a validation\n33\tcampaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware across the supported model set and\n34\tproduces the go/no-go scope — the list of models cleared for productization —\n35\tthat the serving productization work is gated on.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Define the campaign methodology: hardware configuration, ROCm and driver\n40\t  versions, model versions, and serving workload definitions, recorded so the\n41\t  results are reproducible.\n42\t- Execute functional validation: serve each model in the supported model set\n43\t  with vLLM on ROCm and record a pass/fail outcome per model.\n44\t- Execute performance validation: capture serving performance metrics for the\n45\t  same model set against the CUDA baseline builds.\n46\t- Produce the go/no-go recommendation: the parity report and the validated\n47\t  (cleared) model list that productization will build against.\n48\t- Coordinate access to dedicated AMD Instinct nodes (procurement or\n49\t  partner-lab access) as part of the campaign logistics — see Risks.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Functional parity results are recorded for every model in the supported\n54\t  model set, with a pass/fail outcome per model, from vLLM serving runs on\n55\t  physical AMD Instinct hardware.\n56\t- Performance parity data for the same model set is captured against the CUDA\n57\t  baseline, with the comparison metrics documented.\n58\t- The go/no-go recommendation with the cleared model list is published as the\n59\t  campaign report.\n60\t- The campaign methodology (hardware, driver/ROCm versions, model versions,\n61\t  workloads) is documented so the results are reproducible.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- HLR-1 (P0): a validation campaign on physical AMD Instinct hardware\n66\t  establishing functional and performance parity data for vLLM serving of the\n67\t  supported model set, producing the go/no-go scope for productization —\n68\t  fully covered by this epic.\n69\t\n70\t## Risks / Notes\n71\t\n72\t- Hardware access is an availability precondition controlled outside the\n73\t  strategy (procurement or partner-lab negotiation); it is tracked here as a\n74\t  risk rather than an acceptance criterion. The epic's own deliverable is the\n75\t  validated campaign report.\n76\t- Upstream ROCm image cadence is controlled by AMD and the upstream\n77\t  communities; the campaign should pin and record the ROCm versions used so\n78\t  the results are attributable.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b885dddbb438732c","agent_id":"a83ade6d1ea306758","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"cd3f6afc-89cc-4de9-ae98-d993dd0abef5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:32:31.814Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9113c81627934fc9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
