me on AMD Instinct hardware.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- The serving stack exposes the ROCm vLLM runtime as a deployable runtime,\n56\t  referencing the pinned productized ROCm runtime image (the image is\n57\t  produced by the runtime productization work; its availability is an\n58\t  acceptance gate here, not a blocking dependency).\n59\t- An InferenceService deploying a cleared model on the ROCm runtime reaches\n60\t  Ready and serves inference requests successfully on AMD Instinct nodes.\n61\t- InferenceService pods requesting AMD GPU resources are scheduled and run on\n62\t  AMD Instinct nodes.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the\n67\t  models the validation campaign clears — this epic covers the serving-stack\n68\t  integration that makes the productized runtime deployable and usable end\n69\t  to end.\n70\t\n71\t## Risks / Notes\n72\t\n73\t- Gated on the validation campaign outcome: scope follows the cleared model\n74\t  list; a full no-go removes this scope.\n75\t- The strategy lists KServe as an affected component without detailing the\n76\t  change; this epic is scoped at the functional level (runtime exposure and\n77\t  accelerator resource handling), leaving implementation decisions to the\n78\t  team.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b885dddbb438732c","agent_id":"a83ade6d1ea306758","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"bc9a2f93-0a41-4617-a6a9-b07decc68bff","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:32:34.894Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4b2f67546d9fd7d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
