orch image runs to successful\n54\t  completion on AMD Instinct nodes.\n55\t- A multi-GPU (multi-worker) PyTorchJob runs to successful completion with\n56\t  AMD GPUs allocated across the workers.\n57\t- Training jobs produce correct results (job success criteria met, e.g. loss\n58\t  convergence on a reference workload).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU\n63\t  jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic\n64\t  covers the Training Operator side (job execution on ROCm).\n65\t\n66\t## Risks / Notes\n67\t\n68\t- Validation requires access to AMD Instinct hardware — an availability\n69\t  precondition shared with the serving validation campaign and controlled\n70\t  outside the strategy (procurement or partner lab).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9de89d4b90f159fc","agent_id":"ae9b5302a9136331a","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"ba293a33-79ed-49c0-a5d1-cbc8bc35328c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:36:47.111Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9ce0150a31ba1ca","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
