{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14913ea5aa4b231","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9020 (AMD GPU / ROCm enablement for serving and training)\n10\t\n11\tThe strategy was not triaged in Step 0: it spans four components and two owning\n12\tteams, mixes P0/P1/P2 requirements, and its P0 core (the validation campaign)\n13\tis a genuine unknown gating the productization work. It is not documentation-\n14\tonly: the Serving Runtimes, KServe, Training Operator, and Distributed\n15\tWorkloads components all require code or configuration changes.\n16\t\n17\tTeam assignments are inferred from the architecture context files\n18\t(`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/`), because the strategy\n19\thas no Impacted Teams table: KServe and Serving Runtimes are owned by RHOAI\n20\tServing; Training Operator and Distributed Workloads are owned by the\n21\tDistributed Workloads team.\n22\t\n23\t## Epic List\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n26\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E001 | AMD Instinct validation campaign for vLLM ROCm serving | Investigation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E002 | Productize the vLLM ROCm serving runtime for validated models | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E003 | KServe serving-stack enablement for AMD GPU (ROCm) serving | Implementation | RHOAI Serving | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E004 | PyTorch ROCm training support via the Training Operator | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E005 | Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-9020-E006 | Document AMD GPU (ROCm) support | Implementation (docs