upstream ROCm runtime image\n52\t  releases align with platform release trains.\n53\t- License scanning of the ROCm runtime image, covering the new AMD/ROCm\n54\t  transitive dependencies the build introduces.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The ROCm vLLM runtime image builds and its build/test/release pipeline\n59\t  completes green.\n60\t- The runtime image is published through the platform release process for the\n61\t  cleared model set.\n62\t- The runtime serves each cleared model successfully on AMD Instinct hardware,\n63\t  with functional checks recorded per model.\n64\t- The base ROCm image is pinned, and a documented release-alignment note\n65\t  states how upstream ROCm image cadence maps to platform release trains.\n66\t- The license scan of the ROCm runtime image passes, or any exceptions are\n67\t  documented and approved.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-2 (P0): a supported vLLM ROCm serving runtime productized for the\n72\t  models the validation campaign clears — this epic delivers the runtime\n73\t  image itself; the serving-stack exposure that makes it deployable is a\n74\t  separate unit of work on the KServe side.\n75\t\n76\t## Risks / Notes\n77\t\n78\t- Gated on the validation campaign outcome: this epic proceeds with the\n79\t  cleared model list; a full no-go removes the productization scope.\n80\t- Upstream ROCm build cadence is outside our control and may not align with\n81\t  release trains; recorded as a schedule risk and addressed by the pinning\n82\t  and release-alignment acceptance criterion above.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad37a481215dedbe","agent_id":"a2d6f3ce0b73d0bc8","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"dcec281c-1d34-490d-9a86-594ac8287138","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:37:53.807Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8debdae7bae12bd5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","tas