{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-834de64b34b2ed5f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9020-E005\n3\ttitle: Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9020\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Kueue quota handling for amd.com/gpu training workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers amd.com/gpu quota handling in the platform's queueing\n34\tlayer so that ROCm training jobs requesting AMD GPU resources are admitted\n35\tthrough Kueue under the ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, with gang\n36\t(all-or-nothing) admission semantics preserved for multi-GPU jobs.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Quota and resource-flavor coverage for the amd.com/gpu resource in Kueue\n41\t  queueing, following the existing NVIDIA GPU quota handling as the pattern.\n42\t- Preservation of all-or-nothing (gang) admission semantics for multi-GPU\n43\t  jobs requesting amd.com/gpu.\n44\t- End-to-end admission validation: PyTorchJobs requesting amd.com/gpu are\n45\t  admitted against quota covering that resource and run on ROCm nodes.\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A PyTorchJob requesting amd.com/gpu resources is admitted through Kueue\n50\t  against a quota that covers amd.com/gpu.\n51\t- All-or-nothing admission semantics hold for multi-GPU amd.com/gpu jobs: a\n52\t  job is admitted only when its full GPU allocation can be satisfied.\n53\t- Admitted amd.com/gpu jobs run on AMD Instinct nodes.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-3 (P1): PyTorch training on ROCm supported for single- and multi-GPU\n58\t  jobs admitted through Kueue, with amd.com/gpu quota handling — this epic\n59\t  covers the queueing/quota side of the requirement.\n60\t\n61\t## Risks / Notes\n62\t\n63\t- End-to-end admission validation requires ROCm training jobs to be runnable\n64\t  (Training Operator side) and access to AMD Instinct hardware — an\n65\t  availability precondition controlled outside the strategy.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad37a481215dedbe","agent_id":"a2d6f3ce0b73d0bc8","session_id":"da64fd2d-69d4-4f10-98cf-a5e53b041b70","uuid":"741b5981-9e33-43c8-bbab-fc0e579bc985","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:37:59.870Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-834de64b34b2ed5f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9020 decomposition"}
